observed = "The Agent API declares many operation fields only by name (for example prepare.required and read.balance.request_required) without a field-level schema type. The JVM generator emits operation-specific records and preserves those exact required field names, but represents only these under-specified fields as JsonNode. Declared scalars and Human API field:type declarations generate concrete BigInteger, ProtocolAmount, enum, record and list types; the implementation does not infer money or identifier types from field spelling."
assumption = "A future additive Agent schema revision may attach field types to the existing names, at which point regeneration can narrow the corresponding JsonNode components without inventing wire semantics now. Human qualification should treat the remaining JsonNode components as a source-schema limitation rather than full field typing."
severity = "schema-ambiguity"

