observed = "Every existing adapter crate depends on layerx-interop-gateway for neutral descriptor, trace and translation contracts. Making that same crate depend on x402, AP2, UCP, Visa and fiat would create a Cargo dependency cycle. The executable is therefore a dedicated composition crate that depends on the neutral gateway core, every adapter and the hosted gateway library; the required transport-neutral server and interop_gateway_routes symbols remain in layerx-interop-gateway. Adapter registration is validated and then the temporary registry core is dropped before serving, so request state is not duplicated into its in-memory store."
assumption = "The package split is the architecture boundary implied by the task but not represented in its original three-file touch list. Human qualification will treat layerx-interop-service's layerx-interop-gateway binary as the production executable and confirm no adapter dependency is reversed."
severity = "scope-clarification"

[observation.22.4.2]
task = "22.4"
file = "interop/crates/layerx-ap2/src/adapter.rs, platform/hosted/gateway/src/lib.rs, interop/crates/layerx-interop-service/src/server.rs"
symbol = "LayerXIntentPlane::compile, POST /v1/activities, ap2"
observed = "The AP2 adapter's execution trait requires an in-process CompiledIntent and receipt-signing HSM boundary, while the only production hosted gateway contract accepts a caller-signed canonical activity and does not expose a remote CompiledIntent or AP2 receipt-JWT signing endpoint. The executable therefore runs the real AP2 mandate verifier and constraint binding, submits only an already signed canonical activity through the real hosted gateway, and independently matches the returned receipt to the verified mandate amount and deployment asset/accounts. It does not invent a CompiledIntent, payload bytes or an AP2 receipt-signing key."
assumption = "Qualification must decide whether the production core will publish a versioned remote typed-intent/AP2 receipt-signing contract. Until one exists, AP2 terminal success is limited to the receipt-verified LayerX result and mandate identifiers; the executable cannot export AP2 Payment/Checkout Receipt JWTs without a declared signer service."
severity = "dependency-boundary"

[observation.22.4.3]
task = "22.4"
file = "platform/hosted/gateway/src/store.rs, interop/Cargo.lock"
symbol = "RedisStore::operation, gateway:idem principal field, interop workspace lock"
observed = "Durable operation resumption requires binding every idempotency record to its authenticated principal, so new reservations persist a principal field and resume refuses records without the exact principal digest. Redis records created by the earlier hosted gateway schema do not contain that field and intentionally fail closed rather than becoming cross-principal readable. Adding the executable workspace member also changes the Cargo dependency graph, but no build, dependency resolution, lock refresh or qualification command was permitted in this implementation phase."
assumption = "Deployment qualification will drain or explicitly migrate pre-field pending Redis records and regenerate/review interop/Cargo.lock using the pinned dependency graph before building. It must exercise restart, replay and cross-principal resume against Redis AOF persistence."
severity = "phase-boundary"

[observation.22.4.4]
task = "22.4"
file = "interop/crates/layerx-x402/src/lib.rs, interop/crates/layerx-interop-service/src/server.rs, platform/hosted/gateway/src/lib.rs, platform/hosted/gateway/src/store.rs"
symbol = "PinnedSpec::verify_document, verified_x402_transfer, VerifiedTransfer, DurableContinuation"
observed = "Adapter registration embeds each vendored upstream document and refuses a digest mismatch before serving. x402 verification now accepts only a canonical signed Asset SEND or RECEIVE activity from the authenticated signer whose disclosed 402LXP asset, recipient, amount and protocol idempotency key exactly match the payment requirements; settlement submits under that activity idempotency key, binds the returned receipt to the submitted activity and independently matches the receipt transfer facts. Pending operations persist the original bounded request as Redis bulk-safe chunks and redispatch it under a current credential and the same principal-scoped idempotency identity after restart."
assumption = "Human qualification must alter each embedded vendor document, substitute signer, asset, recipient, amount, activity and idempotency fields, exercise MCP and A2A x402 values without private envelopes, and replay pending GET and POST operations across Redis AOF restart, credential rotation, conflicting retries and cross-principal access. No build, test, format or runtime result is asserted by this implementation task."
severity = "qualification-required"

[observation.32.6.6]
task = "32.6"
file = "cmd/layerxd/lxp_daemon_batch_wal.c, cmd/layerxd/lxp_daemon_batch_wal.h, cmd/layerxd/lxp_daemon_process.c"
symbol = "lxp_daemon_batch_wal_write_prepared, lxp_daemon_batch_wal_transition, lxp_daemon_batch_wal_retire"
observed = "Adversarial storage review found that the first prepared-batch WAL capped the entire record at the protocol body limit without reserving its fixed metadata and sixty-four Merkle-proof overheads, could strand progress on orphan temporary names, released its cooperative directory lock before completing a read and allowed prepare or terminal transition to replace an unresolved different marker. The repaired format uses an explicit bounded body-plus-overhead cap, unique anchored temporary names with locked orphan sweeping, holds the directory lock through full reads, requires absence for a new PREPARED record, byte-compares the exact current PREPARED record under the same lock before terminal replacement and durably retires only an exact terminal record at its permitted live boundary."
assumption = "The checkpoint directory filesystem must provide the file and directory fsync, rename, openat, no-follow and advisory-lock semantics used by the WAL protocol. Human qualification must fill records to the exact body and proof bounds, inject crashes at every file write, sync, rename, transition and unlink, leave colliding and malformed temporary names, race cooperative processes and verify that no unresolved marker is overwritten or mistaken for another batch. No filesystem durability, capacity or concurrency result is asserted by the source implementation."
severity = "wal-filesystem-assumption"

[observation.32.6.7]
task = "32.6"
file = "cmd/layerxd/lxp_daemon_protocol.c, cmd/layerxd/lxp_daemon_process.c, src/modules/programs/feed_store.c, include/layerx/programs.h"
symbol = "lxp_programs_state_feed_store_open, lxp_programs_state_feed_store_anchor, recover_prepared_batch_wal"
observed = "Final crash-recovery review found that automatically anchoring an absent state-feed log from the already-settled live snapshot before authenticating and classifying a PREPARED or COMMITTED batch WAL makes the recovered receipt sequence precede the feed baseline and permanently prevents observer replay. The repaired startup contract separates recovery of an existing feed from explicit first anchoring: WAL authentication and context validation precede any anchor, an absent feed is anchored at the live boundary's receipt-state root when there is no settled WAL to replay and at the authenticated WAL base receipt-state root before replaying a settled batch. The canonical full-state root is a different domain and is never a feed baseline."
assumption = "Human crash qualification must remove only the feed log while retaining each base, PREPARED, ABORTED and COMMITTED WAL/checkpoint combination, inject invalid and context-mismatched WALs, and prove that invalid evidence cannot choose a durable feed baseline while valid settled evidence replays exactly once. No restart or filesystem result is asserted by this implementation phase."
severity = "crash-recovery-ordering"

[observation.17.6.1]
