[observation.37.1.5]
task = "37.1"
file = "paxeer-network/sdk/x/bank/keeper/send.go, paxeer-network/engine/deps/xbank/keeper/send.go, paxeer-network/sdk/x/bank/keeper/msg_server.go, paxeer-network/modules/epoch/types/hooks.go, paxeer-network/modules/epoch/types/genesis.go, paxeer-network/modules/epoch/genesis.go, paxeer-network/modules/mint/keeper/keeper.go, paxeer-network/sdk/x/staking/genesis.go, paxeer-network/node/app.go, paxeer-network/rpc/simulate.go, paxeer-network/rpc/tx.go, paxeer-network/parallelization/staking/src/contract.rs"
symbol = "SendCoinsAndWei, msgServer.MultiSend, panicCatchingEpochHook, DefaultGenesis, InitGenesis, Keeper.GetOrUpdateLatestMinter, staking.InitGenesis, Backend.GetBlockContext, delegate"
observed = "Post-implementation review found negative or uninitialized fractional transfer amounts could panic or increase balances, mixed coin and fractional transfers could leave partial writes, direct send and multisend invocation trusted non-nil upstream messages while multisend also panic-parsed addresses, and zero-value fractional no-ops were ordered after recipient rejection. Epoch hooks swallowed consensus-critical panics while epoch processing continued, default epoch genesis used local wall-clock time, an absent mint schedule was dereferenced, staking genesis ignored index errors and terminated the process on validator-update failure, RPC tracing returned an empty block context as success and trusted concrete state and decoded transaction shapes, the staking contract indexed absent funds, and an unfinished wasm migration was registered as a hard fork at a fixed height. The repair rejects invalid amounts and messages before mutation, preserves the documented initialized zero-transfer no-op, commits mixed transfers atomically, propagates hook and initialization failures, derives default epoch time from consensus context, validates staking genesis inputs before writes, fails RPC conversion and context construction explicitly, validates staking funds, and removes the placeholder hard-fork registration and implementation. Module migration-registration errors for bank, staking, mint and tokenfactory are now fatal during application wiring instead of ignored."
assumption = "Human qualification must run the bank, epoch, mint, staking, tokenfactory, RPC and contract suites; inject failed coin writes after fractional staging, malformed genesis keys and addresses, panicking hooks, missing block time, unsupported tracer state, malformed EVM messages and invalid staking funds; and prove application startup rejects duplicate migration registration. No build, test, formatting, migration replay or passing result is asserted by this source repair."
severity = "post-implementation-repair"

[observation.37.1.6]
task = "37.1"
file = "paxeer-network/consensus/autobahn/types/committee.go, paxeer-network/consensus/autobahn/types/msg.go, paxeer-network/consensus/autobahn/types/proposal.go, paxeer-network/consensus/internal/p2p/giga_router.go"
symbol = "Committee.Leader, SecretKey.ForCommittee, Sign, Signed.VerifySig, Proposal.checkedGlobalRange, Proposal.NextTimestamp"
observed = "Post-implementation review found Autobahn used one process-wide signature tag for every network and committee, selected leaders from only the view coordinates, and converted attacker-controlled proposal block counts to time.Duration without a checked bound. A valid vote, proposal, timeout or quorum certificate could therefore be replayed wherever the same validator key was accepted, while oversized lane ranges could wrap global block or timestamp arithmetic. The repair derives a canonical committee domain from the verifier-owned chain ID, genesis boundary, first block, ordered validator keys and weights; binds local validator keys to that domain at router construction; includes explicit operation domains in signature, leader and shard preimages; rejects unbound signing; and checks lane aggregation, committee offsets and timestamp steps before proposal production or acceptance."
assumption = "Human qualification must run Autobahn type, consensus, availability, persistence, data and router suites; replay serialized votes and quorum certificates across different chain IDs, first blocks and validator weights; restart over existing WAL state with the identical genesis; and inject maximum lane and timestamp offsets. No build, test, formatting, network or passing result is asserted by this source repair."
severity = "post-implementation-repair"

