symbol = "decode, migrate_legacy, DepositProofIdentity, DepositPlan::paxeer_chain_id"
observed = "The custody-root repair changed the durable proof identity without an explicit reader for version-1 deposit records and reused the binding NetworkId u32 as the Paxeer JSON-RPC chain identity. The follow-up introduces record version 3 with explicit current, legacy-v1 and legacy-v2 schemas. Terminal legacy Done and Failed histories remain readable with their original failure or an explicitly tagged LegacyProofCommitment; incomplete legacy phases become the terminal LegacyProofSchema status and retain their original phase without being resumed under the new verifier. A mutable journey access rewrites the migrated representation durably. Paxeer chain identity is now a separate nonzero u64 throughout the plan, wallet request, durable record, versioned plan digest and proof comparison; the wallet binding scope and LayerX network remain distinct u32 values."
assumption = "Human qualification must replay real version-1 records for every phase, prove Done and Failed history is byte-accounted and incomplete records cannot create another wallet or credit effect, exercise restart after migration, reject inconsistent legacy activity evidence, and use a Paxeer chain ID above u32::MAX through wallet submission and finality proof comparison. No build, migration execution, test, formatting, install, network call or passing result is asserted by this source repair."
severity = "durability-boundary"

